We measure LLM probability updates on δ-SNLI premise–hypothesis pairs across the Multi-Candidate Verbalization (MCV) family. Separate calls elicit priors and posteriors; directional movement s signs changes by the annotated direction. We cross stated versus reported wording with Direct single estimates (D0) versus Multi-Candidate Weighted elicitation (MCW; five weighted estimates, V0, weighted mean M\_W). Frozen formal tests cover 15 configurations (23,400 planned units): 3 primary (Qwen3-8B thinking off, OLMo-2-7B, gpt-6.1-sol via codex; 6,600), 4 CLI-harnessed configurations (gpt-oss-120b, claude-sonnet-5.5, gemini-3.8-flash low/high; dnli-agy; 5,600), and 8 un-harnessed REST API configurations (dnli-api; 11,200). We add a 20-configuration, eight-provider dev ladder (3B–550B; 6,000 units) and a two-model OpenAI 1+1+4 ablation of D0, Direct-CoT (D\_CoT), MCW (V0), and Multi-Candidate Unweighted (MCU; V2 / M\_U; 1,800 calls). All 15 reject H1 (s = +16.1 to +28.9 points) and H4a (endpoint reduction +0.065 to +0.391); 13 reject H2 (+2.0 to +8.9 points), except gpt-oss-120b (+0.9) and sf:qwen3.5-4b (−0.64). In 14 of 15 formal configurations, readouts obey Top-1 \> MCW (M\_W) \> MCU (M\_U). On 120 common pairs, API Qwen3 tracks local Qwen3 (H1 +18.72 vs. +18.90; H4a +0.265 vs. +0.254; H2 +3.78 vs. +1.67; H4b −9.03 vs. −6.70); local H2 rejects on all 240 pairs (+1.97), not this subset. API Gemma 31B (formal H4b −2.85, Top-1 +0.64; spread −13.3% / +7.6%) and Groq gpt-oss-120b (dev −4.15, +0.40; −18.4% / +12.2%) show small MCW costs and stated narrowing/reported widening without CLI harnesses. In OpenAI ablations, D\_CoT keeps numeric-token entropy \<1 bit; MCU (V2) recovers movement but halves spread and ΔH2 vs. MCW (V0). Because δ-NLI annotates only direction, we make no claim about appropriate update magnitude. Code/data: https://github.com/asj252/llm-judgment-studies
